# Recipe: offline-first app

Use `/data` `openCollection` for new single-writer shared JSON, or
`openCollaborativeDatabase` with explicit writer approval for collaboration.
Read `modules/managed-data.mdc` and the `p2p-data-sync` recipe.

Local open and data access must not wait for announcement or remote peers.
Show locally available data immediately. Run bounded sync/network waits as an
explicit background or sharing action; report timeouts and honor cancellation.
Reopen the same dataset directory after restart to retain keys and local data.

Keep credentials/device-private state outside replicated storage. Preserve an
existing local database and its replication manager instead of silently opening
it with a managed helper. Do not add manual Hyperswarm replication around `/data`.
Test startup with no peers, offline edits for authorized writers, restart,
reconnect/convergence and clean shutdown. Collaboration remains experimental;
local receipts do not prove remote durability.
